flowchart TB
    accTitle: Reveal or copy one password
    accDescr: A protected desktop read uses the current login. Table-locked actions prompt for the Master Password and always relock in finally before delivering a result. Lifecycle changes discard stale results. Clipboard writes recheck authorization and attempt owned-value cleanup after 30 seconds and on lock.
    action["Select an item\nReveal or Copy password"] --> login{"Login still active?"}
    login -->|No| signin["Sign in again\nMaster Password + Authenticator"]:::danger
    login -->|Yes| locked{"Table locked?"}
    locked -->|No| read["Serialized Core read\nCheck deadlines, ID and item type"]
    locked -->|Yes| prompt["Prompt for Master Password\nNo extra OTP within active login"]
    prompt -->|Cancel / incorrect| stop["Stop without disclosure"]:::danger
    prompt -->|Correct| temporary["Temporarily decrypt vault\nKeep original login deadline"]
    temporary --> protected["Read selected password\nRefresh cached metadata"]
    protected --> relock["finally: lock vault\nEven if the read fails"]
    relock --> current{"Successful result and\nsame authorized lifecycle?"}
    read --> current
    current -->|No| stop
    current -->|Yes| output{"Selected action?"}
    output -->|Reveal| reveal["SECRET: show password dialog"]:::secret
    output -->|Copy| guard["Recheck authorization\nat queued clipboard write"]
    guard -->|Valid| copy["SECRET: Windows clipboard\nTrack ownership and exact value"]:::secret
    guard -->|Stale| stop
    copy --> cleanup["After 30 seconds or on lock:\nbest-effort clear only the owned value"]
    classDef secret fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#d97706,color:#0f172a
    classDef danger fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#991b1b
